---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

title: "Release Notes";
description: "Release history for the Umi‑Time Specification and reference implementations.";
---

<Base title="Release Notes">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-release-notes">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Release Notes</h1>
        <p>
          The Umi‑Time project currently consists of two independently versioned
          artifacts:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            The <strong>Umi‑Time Specification</strong>, which defines the
            standard.
          </li>
          <li>
            The <strong>umi-time</strong> JavaScript library, which serves as the
            reference implementation.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>Release notes for both are maintained on this page.</p>
      </header>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Specification Releases -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="example">
        <h2>Specification Releases</h2>

        <article>
          <h3>Specification v1.0.0 — Initial Public Release</h3>
          <h4>November 1, 2026</h4>

          <p>The first stable release of the Umi‑Time specification.</p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              Establishes the Layer 0 (UTC), Layer 1 (Umi‑Time Representation),
              Layer 2 (Local Interpretation), and Layer 3 (Solar Context)
              architecture.
            </li>

            <li>Defines the 360‑umi representation of the UTC day.</li>

            <li>Defines canonical Umi‑Time formats and representations.</li>

            <li>Defines longitude‑based local interpretation principles.</li>

            <li>
              Defines optional local-interpretation and solar-context layers.
            </li>

            <li>
              Establishes normative terminology, computational rules, and
              conformance requirements.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- JavaScript Reference Implementation Releases -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="example">
        <h2>JavaScript Reference Implementation Releases</h2>

        <article>
          <h3>umi-time v1.0.0 — Initial Stable Release</h3>
          <h4>November 1, 2026</h4>

          <p>
            The first stable release of the official JavaScript reference
            implementation.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>
              First publication of the <code>umi-time</code> npm package.
            </li>

            <li>
              Introduces the immutable <code>UmiTime</code> class.
            </li>

            <li>
              Implements Umi‑Time conversion, parsing, and formatting APIs.
            </li>

            <li>
              Implements Layer 3 solar-context calculations through
              solar-geometry helpers including
              <code>solarAltitude</code>,
              <code>getHourAngle</code>,
              <code>toDeg</code>,
              <code>toRad</code>, and
              <code>utUmiFromDate</code>.
            </li>

            <li>Ships comprehensive TypeScript definitions.</li>

            <li>Provides ESM, CommonJS, and browser‑ready builds.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Semantic Versioning -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="example">
        <h2>Semantic Versioning</h2>

        <p>
          Both the Umi‑Time Specification and the
          <code>umi-time</code> JavaScript library follow semantic versioning (<code
            >MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH</code
          >).
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>MAJOR</strong> versions indicate incompatible changes.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>MINOR</strong> versions introduce new functionality while preserving
            backward compatibility.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>PATCH</strong> versions contain fixes, clarifications, and refinements.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Publication Locations -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="example">
        <h2>Where Releases Are Published</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Specification:</strong>
            GitHub releases and tagged specification updates.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>JavaScript Library:</strong>
            npm package releases and GitHub release tags.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>Website:</strong>
            Release summaries and project announcements.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Feedback -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="example">
        <h2>Feedback</h2>

        <p>
          If you discover an issue, find an ambiguity in the specification, or
          have ideas for future improvements, please open an issue on GitHub or
          visit the <a href="/contributing">Contributing</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
